{{wikipedia}}
==English==

===Etymology===
''ig-'' (from ''[[ignorant]]'') + ''[[gnostic]]'' + ''-[[ism]]''. Coined by [[w:Rabbi Sherwin Wine|Rabbi Sherwin Wine]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# The philosophical position that "the question of the existence of God" is not really a question at all for it is a meaningless phrase since the term "God" has not been assigned any coherent definition. They do not consider "creator of the universe" as coherent language.  Ignostics claim to have no concept of anything that the term "God" could refer to.     

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|igtheism}}

